hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
530,"Ali bin Abi Talib narrated:\It is from the SUnnah to leave for the Eid walking"""
531,"**Narrated by Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him):**\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), Abu Bakr, and 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) used to perform the prayer of the two 'Eids before the sermon (khutbah), after which they would deliver the sermon.\n\n**It is also reported in this chapter from Jabir and Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them).**\n\nAbu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: The hadith of Ibn 'Umar is a *hasan sahih* (good and authentic) hadith. The established practice (*'amal*) among the scholars from the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) and others is that the prayer of the two 'Eids precedes the sermon. It is also said that the first person to deliver the sermon before the prayer was Marwan ibn al-Hakam."
532,"Jabir bin Samurah narrated:\I prayed the two Eid prayers with the Prophet - not one time"""
533,
534,"Ubaidullah bin Abdullah bin Utbah narrated:\Umar bin Al-Khattab asked Abu Waqid Al-Laithi what Allah's Messenger would recite during Al-Fitr and Al-Adha"""
535,Ubaidullah bin Abdullah bin Utbah:There is a another chain with similar narration
536,"# Translation of the Hadith\n\n**Muslim ibn 'Amr Abu 'Amr al-Hadda' al-Madani narrated to us:** 'Abdullah ibn Nafi' al-Sa'igh narrated to us, from Kathir ibn 'Abdullah, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet ﷺ performed *takbir* on the two 'Eids: in the first *rak'ah* he made seven *takbirs* before the recitation, and in the second *rak'ah* he made five *takbirs* before the recitation.\n\nHe said: And in this chapter there are narrations from 'A'isha, Ibn 'Umar, and 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr.\n\nAbu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: The hadith of Kathir's grandfather is a *hasan* hadith, and it is the best thing narrated in this chapter from the Prophet ﷺ. His name is 'Amr ibn 'Auf al-Muzani.\n\nAnd this is the practice upon which some of the people of knowledge acted, from among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ and others. And it is narrated similarly from Abu Hurayra that he prayed in Madinah in a manner close to this prayer, and this is the position of the people of Madinah. Upon this say Malik ibn Anas, al-Shafi'i, Ahmad, and Ishaq.\n\nIt is narrated that 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said regarding the *takbir* on the two 'Eids: in the first *rak'ah* there are five *takbirs* before the recitation, and in the second *rak'ah* one begins with the recitation, then performs four *takbirs* along with the *takbir* of *ruku'*. And something similar to this has been narrated from more than one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, and this is the position of the people of Kufa. Upon this says Sufyan al-Thawri."
537,"Ibn Abbas narrated:""The Prophet went out on the day of Al-Fitr, so he prayed two Rak'ah, then he did not pray before it nor after it"
538,Abu Bakr bin Hafs - and he is Ibn Umar bin Sa'd bin Abi Waqas - narrated about Ibn Umar
539,"Umm Atiyyah narrated:\Allah's Messenger would order the virgins"""
540,"Ahmad ibn Mani' narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassaan, from Hafsah bint Sirin, from Umm Atiyyah, with a similar narration. He said: And in the chapter [there are narrations] from Ibn Abbas and Jabir. Abu Isa said: The hadith of Umm Atiyyah is a hasan sahih hadith.

Some people of knowledge acted upon this hadith and permitted women to go out to the two Eids, while some disliked it. It is narrated from Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak that he said: ""I dislike today the going out of women to the two Eids. If a woman refuses except to go out, then let her husband permit her to go out in her worn-out clothes and not adorn herself. If she refuses to go out in that manner, then the husband has the right to prevent her from going out.""

It is narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: ""If the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) saw what women have innovated, he would have prevented them from the mosque, just as the women of Banu Israel were prevented.""

It is narrated from Sufyan al-Thawri that he disliked today the going out of women to the Eid."
541,"Abu Hurairah narrated:\When Allah's Messenger would go out on the day of Eid by one route"""
542,"Abdullah bin Buraidah narrated from his father:\The Prophet would not leave on the Day of Fitr until he ate"""
543,"Anas bin Malik narrated:\The Prophet would have a breakfast of dates on the Day of Fitr before leaving for the Musalla"""
